{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/1489625-a-larp-nasty-nostalgia","id":1489625,"title":"A LARP Nasty (nostalgia)","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Vampire: The Masquerade"],"posts":[{"date":"2022-08-10T05:29:55-07:00","id":1489625,"title":"A LARP Nasty (nostalgia)","content":"WARNING<br /> The following is a true account from a LARP, which I posted 20 years ago on the old Forums. I thought it would be nice with a bit of nostalgia and hope it isn't perceived as crass or sexist - I'm mainly laughing at my self in it. However, if you're sensitive about such matters as juvenile language and poor acting then read no further.<br /> <br /> <br /> <br /> This tale of epic proportions took place during Easter in 2002 at an RPG Con in the city of Aarhus in Denmark. The legendary forumite, Jackob, had written the LARP which took place in Kabul in the year 1197. The Prince of the city had discovered two powerful artifacts, a book and a dagger, and invited vampires from all over the world to individually bid on them.<br /> Jackob had lured me into playing this this 800-year-old dry and unattractive Cappadocian, who'd spent his last 300 years inside a library in Rome. I had preferred playing someone handsome and splendid, but suffering from the disease \u201cOmnipleasant\u201d I gave in and put on the 'Black Robe O\u2019 No-scoring' and painted my otherwise beautiful face white for the painful ordeal.<br /> <br /> At the game:<br /> <br /> I must admit that Jackob had actually surpassed himself on this one; the music, props and general decoration created a rather convincing atmosphere and the costumes were simply stunning - in fact, some of the costumes were way too stunning; I had just parked my delicate arse near what was supposed to be the 'marked place' when five outrageously fit girlies in hardly any clothes came waltzing in. I could suddenly feel my tired system over-working itself and I cursed the last fourteen beers that had forced their way down my throat the night before. I knew that my white face was unattractive enough as it was - dissolved vertical lines of sweat would certainly not add anything positive to the entire picture.<br /> <br /> One of the girlies came straight over to my table when she noticed me. She was wearing a Cleopathra style transparent dress which left nothing to the imagination. Come sweat! Come horror!!<br /> <br /> Cleo: Greetings, ancient one!<br /> <br /> Me: I'm not THAT old, you know ... it's make-up.<br /> <br /> Cleo: Huh?<br /> <br /> Me: Right, we\u2019ve started \u2026 and greetings to you as well.<br /> <br /> Cleo: Thank you. I have heard you're the man to talk to.<br /> <br /> Me: (desperately trying not to stare at her nipples protruding through the thing she was wearing) Eh ... okay ... what about?<br /> <br /> Cleo: What do you mean &quot;what about?&quot;? The book, of course.<br /> <br /> Me: Book? (going through my character sheet) Hmmm ... Jesus Fuckin' Christ! I have Academics 6 and Linguistics 6!<br /> <br /> Cleo: Huh?<br /> <br /> Me: Nothing ... eh ... right, the book ... yes ... ehm ... what about it?<br /> <br /> Cleo: Well, it so happens that we're ... [part missing due to Vincent paying attention to something else] ... so, we would like your evaluation of it. Would you per chance meet me later?<br /> <br /> Me: Are you talking In Game?<br /> <br /> Cleo: I beg your pardon?<br /> <br /> Me: Oh ... eh \u2026 certainly.<br /> <br /> Cleo: Good. Walk with me, ancient one.<br /> <br /> Me: I'd rather not.<br /> <br /> Cleo: Why?<br /> <br /> Me: (desperately trying to picture my 7th grade math teacher naked) Eh ... I'm comfy as it is here ... besides I'm waiting for my servants.<br /> <br /> Cleo: Okay then ... we'll talk later. (she walks away)<br /> <br /> Me: Don't stare, Vincent! Don't stare!<br /> <br /> Servant: Who are you talking to, great leader?<br /> <br /> Me: Huh? ... oh, there you are ... what kept you?<br /> <br /> Servant: You told us to gather information on the other guests.<br /> <br /> Me: Right ... good ... why don't you gather some more while I go and have a fag, m'kay?<br /> <br /> Servant: Will do.<br /> <br /> As I darted through the many players, constantly staring at the floor, I began to wonder if Jackob had finally surpassed me in the bird-department. How else could he have convinced that many saucy birds to show up in that little clothes? I was almost 'home safe' outside the gaming area when a hand gently grabbed my right arm and made me turn around. To my immense horror I saw a girl in a belly-dancer's outfit standing in front of me. Her curves were nothing less than perfect, and the bra barely covered the nipples on the pair of enormous knockers gently floating on front of me. I made a heavy gasp and spent my last two points of willpower on a 'non-grope' roll.<br /> <br /> Setite: Greetings, ancient one.<br /> <br /> Me: I really wish you'd stop calling me that.<br /> <br /> Setite: Forgive me, I have offended thee.<br /> <br /> Me: [Don't bow! Don't bow!! Oh, Gods, she's bowing!] ... ehh ... think nothing of it ... eh ... gorgeous one.<br /> <br /> Setite: I'm glad, for my mistress has sent me to entertain thee until your meeting later this night.<br /> <br /> Me: Are you being serious?<br /> <br /> Setite: Why, certainly.<br /> <br /> Me: Ehh ... ah fuck, I can't do this! Excuse me, I have things to do.<br /> <br /> Setite: But \u2026<br /> <br /> I ran outside the gaming area and finally got my beloved cigarette. As I was standing there, puffing like a lunatic, Jackob came by.<br /> <br /> Jackob: Hey Vince, how is your mission coming along?<br /> <br /> Me: What mission?<br /> <br /> Jackob: The 'obtaining the book' mission, of course.<br /> <br /> Me: How the bloody hell am I to obtain anything in there? Have you SEEN the Setite camp?<br /> <br /> 